  "id": "rationnine",
  "neon": "#ffb43a",
  "note": "RATION NINE — the municipal ration store on the east side of Ironside Street.\n\nThe queue is the building. Everything a ration store does happens on the pavement, so the\ncomposition is a long canopy on posts with two hatches behind it, and almost nothing else. There\nis nothing to display and nobody is browsing, so there is no shopfront.\n\nThe number is bigger than the name. NINE is what people call it and what is painted on it; the\nfull name is a small plate on the parapet band, the way a municipal building signs itself. The hand\nis stencil and the palette is olive because this is issued, not sold.\n\nThe tile's prose gives the rest: the front wall above the canopy is a hand-painted price board,\nrevised by wiping a column off with a rag, and three trolleys are chained together by the door.\nConcrete piers divide the front into two bays, one per hatch, and the queue rail runs along the\nkerb. The flanks carry high barred windows and the back keeps the louvres.\n\nIt replaces its own arm. `rationnine` is a named arm drawing this one tile, so `replaces` is\nthe revert path: `LEGACY_MODELS` holds the arm and `RENDER_TUNE.legacyArms` puts it back.",
  "pal": "ty_fallow",
  "replaces": "rationnine",
